# SRG-APP-000359-WSR-000065  -  CAT II
# The web server must use a logging mechanism that is configured to provide
# a warning to the ISSO and SA when allocated record storage volume reaches
# 75% of maximum log record storage capacity.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000359-WSR-000065
group:           V-206424
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001855
control_rev5:    AU-5

contribution:    The application sets its own storage floor in server.conf and can raise a
                 scheduled alert with an email recipient list as capacity is approached;
                 both the floor and the alert are configured in the product.

governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           server.conf [diskUsage] minFreeSpace matches ^([1-9][0-9]?(\.[0-9]+)?%|[0-9]{6,}|[1-9][0-9]{4})$
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email.to non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] enableSched equals 1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] alert_condition https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          server.conf [diskUsage] minFreeSpace https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        SMTP relay reachability and mail delivery, which depend on the mail server
                 and the network
external:        The ISSO and SA recipient addresses, which the organization supplies
external:        The size of the storage volume, needed only to confirm an absolute
                 minFreeSpace value; a percentage value expresses 25 percent in the product
external:        Which saved search carries the trigger, which is organization-defined
                 content: a trigger is expressed either by alert_condition or by counttype
                 with relation and quantity, so a test on alert_condition alone reports a
                 finding against a search that is correctly configured the other way.

citation:        web.conf log.access_maxsize min 1 is removed on two counts: nothing in the
                 check text or the fix text ties a web access log rotation ceiling to a 75
                 percent capacity warning, and web.conf.spec:878 makes 0 mean unlimited, so
                 the bound fails the largest allocation. enableSched is added because
                 savedsearches.conf.spec:73-77 defaults it to 0: the criterion as written
                 reported a satisfied alert path - condition set, recipient set - for a
                 saved search that never runs. One limitation to record: the three
                 savedsearches conditions are independent per-key tests and the schema
                 cannot bind them to one stanza, so the assessor must confirm they describe
                 the same saved search.
finding:         The application has no enabled, scheduled alert with a recipient list that
                 warns as log record storage approaches capacity, or its free-space floor
                 is unset.
